<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Islam Karimov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1938–2016</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> Karimov was first secretary of the Communist Party of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbeks">Uzbek</a> SSR from 1989 and declared <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a>'s independence on 31 August 1991. Elected president that December, he ruled Uzbekistan as an authoritarian leader until his death in 2016, suppressing opposition and Islamist movements, and his forces killed many protesters at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andijan">Andijan</a> in 2005.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/islam-karimov.jpg" alt="Islam Karimov" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Helene C. Stikkel · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Islam_karimov_ITN.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
